  {
    "episode_id": 75416,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75416.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "Good afternoon, everybody, and it is great to be with you. So what's my relationship with Joe Biden? I have known Joe Biden for close to 40 years. He and my husband, John, were close friends. They worked together on a lot of issues. I worked with him on a lot of issues. His wife, Jill, is one of my good friends. We all got married around the same time. and quite frankly, Jill and I were two of the first working political spouses. I know that makes them difficult for people. I'm not that old, my friends. I'm seasoned, but I'm not old. It was only a couple of decades ago that it was very unusual for the woman to work and political spouses. It was a total no-no. I was quite heartily criticized as was she when we chose to work. We've had a long relationship. We've been through the ups and downs of lives together. I've seen John and General work on some very, very tough legislative issues. But I know Joe Biden is a really good time man with a heart and a soul. and with empathy and compassion. And that's what I think the country needs right now.",
