    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75416.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "I think that Joe Biden really cares about. He cares about everybody in the United States, but he understands the state like Michigan. You know, four years ago, I was one of the people that said that Donald Trump could win the election. A lot of people thought it was crazy. But Donald Trump came in to Michigan and talked about issues that people on Michigan cared about. They wanted to hear somebody talk about trading. I would call Steve Riccietti who's now in the woodhouse with him and say, you can have bring Joe Biden here. He gets it. He can talk to him. Joe Biden understands working men and women who work hard and they play by the rules. They just want to have a good, secure job. They want to be able to buy a house and live in a good neighborhood, put food on the table, educate their kids, and they have a safe and secure retirement. But the Midwest is the heart and soul of this country and Joe Biden understands the heart and soul of this country.",
