    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "So there's been a lot of talk for a long time. First of all, I want to make it really clear when this is a different pad ago and many years ago. It was not the auto industry that blocked having any kind of mass transportation in southeastern Michigan. And when Moses and some of the other groups were trying to get more mass transportation. And I wrote a very strong statement that all three companies supported in support of the idea. You talked about one of the issues, which is the cost of some kind of metro system. But, you know, we've been trying to build slowly that it's not like a rail system, even between Detroit in Ann Arbor. We're trying to make the Michigan quarter a high speed world where you could even use driverless vehicles to be part of the transportation. That's one, but we do need to figure out how we connect between downtown Detroit and Oakland County and far as Port Huron. And we need to develop a transportation system that a public transportation system that will make it easier. for people to get around. And that takes a will. And that will has to be among community leaders.",
