    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "So I think that first of all, Joe Biden's got a good relationship with the states, many of the governors. The federal government needs to be giving money aid to the states and so that we can help a smaller child. Do you create? What kind of economic zones can you create? What kind of incentives can you create? But there are people that I know that are going into this by the administration. Brian, these who's heading up the Domestic Council was critical on the auto. I hate to use the word bailout, but when when the auto crisis occurred in 2008 and 2009. Brian Dees was one of the people that saves the auto industry. He's in there now as head of the economic council and we've talked about things. I mean, one idea. I've talked to Jennifer Vanholm about this too. You know, we're going to build electric vehicles, but right now 98% of the batteries for electric vehicles are being built in China. We need to build those batteries here in the United States. We need to build those plants. What do we need to? What's the R&D we've got to do to develop even the resources to build that battery? And then we want to build a mirror. But that's taking all of our federal state and local working together to develop those kind of plants.",
