    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75416.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "You mentioned steady. Things are going to be steady and consistent. And you're known to work across party lines. So this past year, we have seen a rise in political extremism throughout Trump era, but more recently. You know, we've seen Republican leaders do things like avoid masks, certain languages used. So I want to know where do you see the GOP's future heading with this new administration given all of these events that have happened this past year? I mean, we already have seen two of our own Republican representatives vote to impeach Trump, but not everyone feels that way. So I'm curious to know what's the future of the Republican Party in",
