    "turn_text": "Yeah, I mean, there were literally tens of thousands, like that's not even really an exaggeration of how people showed up to these things. I mean, I was stuck in the parking lot at one event in Saginaw County for like two hours trying to get home afterward. You know, there are these big airport rallies, which I think is new and we might see something like that continue. So just these two totally different versions for how this is going to go and. I don't know, we just had a really hard time. I feel like getting a sense for where the country was going to go, turn out who was going to be really high. But it ended up being a pretty incredible election in terms of the number of people that came out to vote and embracing a new battle of voting with absentee. And then the election really wasn't over until last week when Biden was inaugurated because these you know, these persistent claims of fraud. It",
