    "turn_idx": 51,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I think that is going to be, you know, he campaigned pretty hard on promising people of color that he would bring more opportunities to them. And I think You know, when I was without talking to people, there were folks that were certainly excited who had that relationship with Biden, that kind of longest sort of relationship that he seems to have had with Black voters throughout his political career. But there were also a lot of people who were like, I don't know, man, he's not Trump, so I'll vote for him. I'm going to really wait to see what he can do before I'm a big fan of his. I think a lot of people are waiting for him to make good on those promises. So I don't know. The one thing I know that he's got a good relationship with officials in Flint and Detroit. I think we could see more federal grants coming their way. I think infrastructure is the big thing. Infrastructure was kind of like this joke in the last administration. It was something that would kept being promised but didn't really go anywhere. You know, he put Pete Buttigieg in charge of the Department of Transportation. He's a Midwest guy. Maybe that means we get some more help here in Michigan to, you know, repair water infrastructure, pipes, aging pipes and, you know, lead, all that stuff. maybe helps with updating, you know, some zoning and building codes. You know, there could be a lot of things that fall under that umbrella. I think people are really looking forward to what he does on climate to environmental justice became a big issue in the last campaign. You know, it kind of like got pushed to the side in the general election wasn't as big of an issue as it was during the Democratic primary, but, you know, Jennifer Granholm, our former governor is going to be if she's confirmed leading the Department of Energy and people are looking for her to bring electric vehicle technology jobs to Detroit boost manufacturing jobs there and also, you know, begin clean up of. some of these contaminated sites. That's more of kind of an EPA job than Department of Energy, but overall climate policy and the environmental justice angle is something people are looking for Biden to get done. So I think those are just a couple of things, but you guys are right to say, I mean, people are kind of waiting to see what he's going to do here. There are some pretty high expectations that, especially with Kamala Harris being with him, that that'll create some new opportunities for folks that have been kind of left behind.",
